{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Reuse Spring XD's existing two-level property mechanism (bus-level properties 'xd.messagebus.<transport>.*' with per-stream/per-module deployment property overrides) for both the Rabbit retry configuration (U2) and the Kafka consumer/producer tuning (U7), registering new property keys in the bus property metadata for validation and shell completion.",
    "For U2, implement retry classification with Spring Retry (SimpleRetryPolicy / ExceptionClassifierRetryPolicy) in RabbitMessageBus: expose a configurable list of retryable/non-retryable exception class names, treat org.springframework.amqp.support.converter.MessageConversionException as non-retryable by default, map org.springframework.messaging.converter.MessageConversionException thrown from module code onto the same non-retryable path at the bus boundary, and add Kryo deserialization failures (com.esotericsoftware.kryo.KryoException) to the default non-retryable set.",
    "For U6, pass module id and container id into each launched module's environment (system properties / PropertySource in the module launch context) and expose them via a ModuleInfo bean so any source/processor/sink can inject them; extend the default logging pattern so log lines include the identifiers.",
    "Dependency upgrades (U3, U4, U5) are done centrally in the Gradle build (dependency management/BOM alignment), keeping public APIs unchanged and fixing only compile/behavioral regressions required by the new versions.",
    "U1 is implemented purely in the AngularJS-based admin UI: a new landing/default route with a view containing higher-order navigation links to sources, processors, sinks and jobs; no new backend REST endpoints are needed.",
    "U8 creates one public Git repository containing parameterized build scripts (Gradle + rpm plugin / spec templates) that produce both the plain XD RPM and the XD + Ambari RPM from shared sources, with CI producing installable artifacts.",
    "Testing approach: JUnit unit tests per change, integration tests against embedded/local RabbitMQ and Kafka brokers, plus execution of the existing regression suite; documentation updates go into the reference guide alongside code changes."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer performs all work; estimates are effort in workdays, not calendar duration, and assume familiarity with the Spring XD codebase, Spring Integration, Spring AMQP and the admin UI stack.",
    "The existing Spring XD code base, build system (Gradle) and CI infrastructure are available and in a working state at the start of the increment.",
    "The dependency upgrades in U3, U4 and U5 are compatible drop-ins requiring only minor code adjustments; no changes in the upstream Spring projects are needed.",
    "Local/embedded RabbitMQ and Kafka brokers (or equivalents) are available for integration testing without additional infrastructure setup effort.",
    "U1 requires only static higher-order navigation links on a landing page; no changes to admin REST APIs, security, or dynamic content aggregation are needed.",
    "For U2, the documented 'never retried' exception is confirmed to be org.springframework.amqp.support.converter.MessageConversionException; the fix also ensures the messaging-converter variant thrown by custom modules stops retries, without re-packaging spring-amqp classes into modules.",
    "For U6, exposing identifiers as environment/system properties and a log-pattern change satisfies the requirement; no persistent audit subsystem is required.",
    "RPM builds target RHEL/CentOS 6/7 style environments; repository hosting (e.g., GitHub) and CI accounts already exist and need no procurement.",
    "Code review is performed by project maintainers; the developer's own effort includes self-review and addressing review feedback (covered in a dedicated rework activity).",
    "No formal project management, requirements elicitation, or release-notes/announcement activities beyond the listed ones are included."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Overall analysis and technical design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze all eight user stories against the current Spring XD codebase, design the shared bus/deployment property override approach for U2 and U7, define new property keys and defaults, decide the ModuleInfo/logging approach for U6, and sketch the admin UI landing page and RPM repo structure. Produces a short design note guiding implementation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Admin UI landing page with higher-order links",
      "activity_description": "Add a landing/default route in the AngularJS admin UI containing higher-order links to the sources, processors, sinks and jobs sections; create the view/controller, adjust routing and navigation, apply basic styling, and add UI-level tests plus manual cross-browser verification.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: Configurable retryable exceptions for RabbitMessageBus",
      "activity_description": "Implement configurable retryable/non-retryable exception classification in RabbitMessageBus using Spring Retry, wire new bus-level and stream deployment-level properties (including property metadata), make AMQP MessageConversionException and Kryo deserialization failures non-retryable by default, and ensure messaging-converter exceptions from custom modules stop retries. Includes unit tests and integration tests against a RabbitMQ broker covering retry and no-retry scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3: Upgrade to Spring Integration 4.1.5",
      "activity_description": "Bump Spring Integration to 4.1.5 in the Gradle dependency management, align related Spring dependencies, resolve compile/deprecation issues, and run the affected unit and integration tests (especially message channel behavior) to confirm no regressions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4: Upgrade to Spring Integration Kafka extension 1.2.0",
      "activity_description": "Upgrade the SI Kafka extension to 1.2.0, adapt KafkaMessageBus code to any API changes, and validate producer/consumer behavior and performance-related paths with the Kafka integration test suite.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5: Upgrade to Spring Hadoop 2.2.0 GA",
      "activity_description": "Upgrade Spring Hadoop to 2.2.0 GA in the build, resolve any configuration or API breakage, and regression-test HDFS-related sinks and jobs against a Hadoop test environment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6: Expose module id and container id to modules",
      "activity_description": "Pass module id and container id into the module launch environment (system properties/PropertySource), provide an injectable ModuleInfo accessor for source/processor/sink developers, update the default logging pattern so identifiers appear in log output, and cover with unit and container-level integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7: Kafka bus consumer and producer property overrides",
      "activity_description": "Add configurable KafkaMessageBus properties autoCommitEnabled, queueSize, maxWait and fetchSize for consumers and batchSize and batchTimeout for producers, with bus-level defaults overridable via stream deployment properties; register property metadata, apply settings to the underlying Kafka consumer/producer factories, and verify behavior with unit and Kafka integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8: Consolidate XD and XD+Ambari RPM scripts into one public repo",
      "activity_description": "Create the single public repository, merge and parameterize the existing XD and XD+Ambari RPM build scripts (spec templates, init scripts, Gradle/rpm build), set up CI build jobs for both artifacts, and validate the produced RPMs with clean installs on target RHEL/CentOS environments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Reference documentation updates",
      "activity_description": "Update the reference guide for all new features: landing page navigation, Rabbit retry configuration properties and the MessageConversionException clarification (U2), the new module/container id logging capability (U6), Kafka consumer/producer properties (U7), upgraded dependency versions (U3-U5), and the unified RPM build repository (U8).",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting integration and regression testing",
      "activity_description": "Run the full existing regression suite plus end-to-end scenarios combining the increment's changes (Rabbit and Kafka buses, module deployment with new properties, admin UI, upgraded libraries) and fix defects found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Code review and rework",
      "activity_description": "Self-review of all changes, preparation of pull requests/patches, and implementation of rework arising from maintainer code review feedback across all stories.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Release build, packaging and final verification",
      "activity_description": "Produce final build artifacts (distribution archives and RPMs), verify install/upgrade paths and smoke-test the complete increment, and tag/prepare the release state in version control.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 51
  }
}

